/public/fighters/
/public/headshots/

# ── Android / Trusted Web Activity build output ─────────────────────────────
# The KEYSTORE is the app's identity. Play will not let you re-key a published
# listing, so a leaked or lost one is unrecoverable in opposite directions:
# leaked means anyone can sign as you, lost means you can never ship an update.
# It belongs in a password manager and a backup, never in git.
*.keystore
*.jks
android/android.keystore
# Bubblewrap writes its own credentials + the generated Gradle project here.
android/*.keystore
android/twa-manifest.json
android/app/
android/gradle*
android/build*
android/.gradle/
android/*.apk
android/*.aab
android/store_icon.png
android/*.iml

# Private evidence / identity documents stored on local disk in dev.
# NEVER tracked: in local development this directory holds real uploads.
.private/
